{title: 253 - There's No Other Name Like Jesus}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #253 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 253}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]There's no other name like Jesus, 'Tis the [C7]dearest name we [F]know,
[F]'Tis the angel's joy in heaven, 'Tis the [C7]Christian's joy [F]below.
[F]Sweet name, dear name, There's no [C7]other name like [F]Jesus;
[F]Sweet name, dear name, There's no [C7]other name like Je[F]sus.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[F]Sweet name, [C7](sweet name) dear [F]name, (dear name)
[F]There's no [C7]other name [F]like Jesus;
[F]Sweet name, [C7](sweet name) dear [F]name, (dear name)
[F]There's no [C7]other name [F]like Jesus.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]There's no [C7]other name [F]like Jesus
[F]When the [C7]heart with [F]grief is sad,
[F]There's no [C7]other name [F]like Jesus
[F]When the [C7]heart is [F]free and glad.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]'Tis the [C7]hope that I [F]shall see Him
[F]When [C7]in glory [F]He appears,
[F]'Tis the [C7]hope to [F]hear His welcome
[F]That [C7]my fainting [F]spirit cheers.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]If He [C7]wills that [F]I should labor
[F]In His [C7]vineyard day [F]by day,
[F]Then 'tis [C7]well if [F]only Jesus
[F]Blesses all [C7]I do [F]or say.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[F]If He [C7]wills that [F]death's cold finger
[F]Touch [C7]my feeble, [F]mortal clay,
[F]Then 'tis [C7]well if [F]only Jesus
[F]Is my [C7]dying trust [F]and stay.
{end_of_verse}
